# iOS Speedflight

Follow the repo skill at `.agents/skills/howmuch-speedflight/SKILL.md` and the runbook at `docs/speedflight.md`. In short:

- Publication requires explicit user authorization — completed iOS work alone does not authorize it. Offer the build when the handoff is obvious; wait for the yes.
- `git fetch origin` and build the exact requested revision (default fetched `origin/main`), never a stale local branch. Set `SPEEDFLIGHT_SOURCE_REF` to the full containing ref.
- Preflight gitignored `.env.speedflight` and the Tinkertanker (`PQ6U5ESLN2`) `.p8`; never switch `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` to T Krobot. On any failed check, stop and report the remedy from the runbook's blocker table.
- Post the Speedflight page URL only in the private chat, never in PRs, issues, or public logs.
